  "_comment": [
    "Craftpix '2D RPG Desert Tileset' (free), added by the user on 2026-08-15.",
    "",
    "NOT PIXEL ART AS SHIPPED. Vector sources (.ai/.eps), 200-560px sprites,",
    "800-1100 distinct colours each, soft drop shadows baked into alpha. Every",
    "entry below is a TARGET SIZE for tools/desert-pixelate.py, which converts",
    "rather than crops. Read that file's docstring before changing anything here.",
    "",
    "SIZES ARE CHOSEN AGAINST THE VALLEY'S OWN SPRITES, not against the source.",
    "The map is TILE=16, and its existing buildings run houseRed 72x101,",
    "churchStone 94x115, cfHouse 96x128, with instAcademic 245x107 as the one",
    "landmark-scale piece. Desert buildings are pitched into that same band so a",
    "desert street reads at the same scale as a valley street. Widths are set and",
    "heights follow the source aspect ratio, so nothing is squashed.",
    "",
    "colours / flatten ARE CALIBRATED, NOT GUESSED. The measure is mean",
    "horizontal colour-run length — how far you travel before the colour changes.",
    "Cute Fantasy houses sit at 2.0-2.4, tree_autumn at 3.1, rock_big at 4.1. The",
    "first pass of this conversion put palms at 1.28 and cacti at 1.31: the same",
    "palette SIZE as the valley art but sprayed across it instead of blocked, which",
    "is exactly what reads as 'not pixel art'. Foliage therefore gets flatten:true",
    "(a 3x3 median before quantising) which lands it at ~2.0-2.1. Buildings do not:",
    "the filter eats window mullions, and 14 colours alone already puts them at",
    "2.2-2.4, dead centre of the valley band.",
    "",
    "LICENCE: craftpix.net/file-licenses/ — the pack ships only that URL, no",
    "terms text. Free-licence Craftpix assets may be used in games including",
    "commercial ones; REDISTRIBUTING the assets themselves is not allowed. That",
    "matters here because a website serves the sprite files directly. Same",
    "unresolved question HANDOFF §9.10 already records for Pixel 16 and",
    "TopDownFantasy_Forest. Worth settling before the site ships.",
    "",
    "Regenerate: python tools/desert-pixelate.py --sheet --compare"
  ],

